<title>DENMARK: Danish August North Sea gas production down 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish August North Sea gas production down 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) production of gas from its North Sea fields fell 10 percent to 347 million cubic metres in August from 387 million cubic metres in July, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>    (Million cubic metres)   Aug 96     July 96   Aug 95</p>
<p>    Total production	    347	   387	 236</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the third-biggest producer in western Europe after Norway and Britain.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively.</p>
<p>--Uffe Hansen, Copenhagen Newsroom 45-33-969656</p>
</text>
